Q: How to load structs from a text file with fixed multi-line records in C A: <p>There is no <em>´correct and idiomatic way in C to load records that span multiple lines´</em>, you need to implement a solution that works for the data you are working with.</p>
<p>In this case one solution would be to read 3 consecutive lines at once by using 3 fgets as part of the condition of a loop, as suggested by @pmg in the comments.</p>
<p>So, the <code>load_data()</code> function could be rewritten as:</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>void load_data()
{
    FILE *data_file = fopen(&quot;data.txt&quot;, &quot;r&quot;);

    while (
        task_counter &lt; MAX_TASKS &amp;&amp;
        fgets(todo_list[task_counter].title, MAX_TITLE_SIZE, data_file) &amp;&amp; 
        fgets(todo_list[task_counter].description, MAX_DESCRIPTION_SIZE, data_file) &amp;&amp;
        fgets(todo_list[task_counter].date, MAX_DATE_SIZE, data_file)
    ) {
        todo_list[task_counter].title[strcspn(todo_list[task_counter].title, &quot;\r\n&quot;)] = '\0';
        todo_list[task_counter].description[strcspn(todo_list[task_counter].description, &quot;\r\n&quot;)] = '\0';
        todo_list[task_counter].date[strcspn(todo_list[task_counter].date, &quot;\r\n&quot;)] = '\0';
        task_counter++;
    }

    fclose(data_file);
}
</code></pre>
<p>Where the <code>while</code> loop condition is satisfied only if the maximum number of tasks hasn't been reached, and the data of all 3 fields (title, description and date) of the task have been successfully read from the data file.</p>
